# Hash-pinned / byte-identity official fixtures.
#
# These artifacts are pinned by SHA-256 in the test suites
# (tests/compliance/test_goaml_schema.py, tests/connectors/rails/
# test_rtgs_official_xsd.py, tests/qr/test_official_vectors.py).
# With core.autocrlf=true on Windows, git rewrites line endings on
# checkout, which breaks byte-identity / sha256 assertions. Treat them
# as binary (-text) so git NEVER touches their bytes on any platform.

tests/fixtures/official/** -text

# Defensive: any extracted-markdown fixture is a byte-pinned artifact.
*.extracted.md -text